# Timepicker Component

## Purpose & Scope

`Timepicker` is a compound component for time selection in the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible time input with:

- **Two display variants**: `inputField` (form-style with floating label) and `compactField` (pill-style button)
- **Compound component pattern**: `Timepicker.Label`, `Timepicker.Field`, `Timepicker.ClockIcon`, `Timepicker.CompactFieldDisplay` subcomponents
- **Native picker integration**: Uses `@react-native-community/datetimepicker` for platform-native time selection
- **Controlled and uncontrolled modes**: Supports both `value` (controlled) and `defaultValue` (uncontrolled)
- **Built-in states**: focus, error, disabled, readonly
- **Floating label animation**: Animated label that floats when focused or filled (inputField variant)
- **Context-based state sharing**: No prop drilling, all state shared via React Context
- **12h/24h format support**: Display in 12-hour (AM/PM) or 24-hour format
- **Configurable minute intervals**: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 10, 12, 15, 20, or 30 minute intervals

**Does NOT handle:**

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Form submission logic (handle in parent)
- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Custom time picker UI (uses native platform pickers)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `Timepicker` (main component - context provider)

```tsx
<Timepicker
  variant?: TimepickerVariant            // 'inputField' | 'compactField' (default: 'inputField')
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>           // Container style override
  defaultValue?: TimeValue | null        // Initial value for uncontrolled mode
  value?: TimeValue | null               // Value for controlled mode
  onChange?: (time: TimeValue | null) => void
  format?: TimeFormat                    // '12h' | '24h' (default: '24h')
  minuteInterval?: number                // 1-30 (default: 1)
  error?: string | null                  // Error state (affects label/border styling, auto-renders helper text)
  disabled?: boolean                     // Disabled state (default: false)
  readonly?: boolean                     // Read-only state (default: false)
>
  {children}
</Timepicker>
```

**Children constraints (inputField variant):**

- Must contain `Timepicker.Label` and `Timepicker.Field` at minimum
- Optional: `Timepicker.ClockIcon` (automatically rendered if not provided)
- Helper text is automatically rendered when `error` exists - do not include it in JSX
- Order matters for visual layout

**Children constraints (compactField variant):**

- Optional: `Timepicker.CompactFieldDisplay` for customization (automatically rendered if not provided)
- Does NOT use `Timepicker.Label`, `Timepicker.Field`, or `Timepicker.ClockIcon`
- Helper text is automatically rendered when `error` exists

### `Timepicker.Label`

```tsx
<Timepicker.Label
  required?: boolean            // Shows asterisk if required
>
  {string}                      // Label text (e.g., "Time" or "Time (Read only)")
</Timepicker.Label>
```

### `Timepicker.Field`

```tsx
<Timepicker.Field
  placeholder?: string
  ref?: Ref<TextInput>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
  accessibilityHint?: string
/>
```

**Note:** The field is always readonly - it displays the formatted time and opens the picker on press. All time-related props (`value`, `defaultValue`, `format`, etc.) are set on the `Timepicker` root component, not on `Timepicker.Field`.

### `Timepicker.ClockIcon`

```tsx
<Timepicker.ClockIcon
  iconName?: string             // Default: 'calendar'
  size?: number                  // Default: 20
  color?: string                 // Optional color override
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string   // Default: 'Open time picker'
/>
```

**Note:** The clock icon is automatically rendered if not provided. It opens the native time picker when pressed. Only used with `inputField` variant.

### `Timepicker.CompactFieldDisplay`

```tsx
<Timepicker.CompactFieldDisplay
  showIcon?: boolean            // Show icon (default: true)
  iconName?: string             // Icon name (default: 'calendar')
  testID?: string               // Default: 'timepicker-compact-field-display'
  accessibilityLabel?: string   // Default: 'Time picker, current value {value}'
/>
```

**Note:** Only used with `compactField` variant. The `CompactFieldDisplay` is automatically rendered if not provided. When no time is selected, displays the format hint string.

### Types

| Type                | Values                               |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `TimepickerVariant` | `'inputField'` \| `'compactField'`   |
| `TimeFormat`        | `'12h'` \| `'24h'`                   |
| `TimeValue`         | `{ hours: number; minutes: number }` |

## Usage Patterns

### Variants Overview

The timepicker supports two display variants:

| Variant        | Description                          | Use Cases                                        |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `inputField`   | Form-style input with floating label | Forms, detailed data entry, validation-heavy UIs |
| `compactField` | Pill-style button                    | Filters, compact layouts, inline time selection  |

### InputField Variant (default)

#### Basic timepicker (uncontrolled)

```tsx
<Timepicker defaultValue={null}>
  <Timepicker.Label>Time</Timepicker.Label>
  <Timepicker.Field placeholder="Select time" />
</Timepicker>
```

#### Controlled timepicker

```tsx
const [time, setTime] = useState<TimeValue | null>(null);

<Timepicker value={time} onChange={setTime}>
  <Timepicker.Label>Time</Timepicker.Label>
  <Timepicker.Field placeholder="Select time" />
</Timepicker>;
```

#### With error state

```tsx
<Timepicker defaultValue={null} error="Please select a valid time">
  <Timepicker.Label>Time</Timepicker.Label>
  <Timepicker.Field />
</Timepicker>
```

#### With 12-hour format

```tsx
<Timepicker defaultValue={null} format="12h">
  <Timepicker.Label>Time</Timepicker.Label>
  <Timepicker.Field />
</Timepicker>
```

#### Disabled and readonly states

```tsx
// Disabled
<Timepicker disabled defaultValue={{ hours: 9, minutes: 30 }}>
  <Timepicker.Label>Time</Timepicker.Label>
  <Timepicker.Field />
</Timepicker>

// Readonly
<Timepicker readonly defaultValue={{ hours: 9, minutes: 30 }}>
  <Timepicker.Label>Time (Read only)</Timepicker.Label>
  <Timepicker.Field />
</Timepicker>
```

### CompactField Variant

#### Basic compact timepicker

```tsx
<Timepicker variant="compactField" defaultValue={null} />
```

When no time is selected, the format hint (e.g., "HH:mm") is shown as a hint.

#### Controlled compact timepicker

```tsx
const [time, setTime] = useState<TimeValue | null>(null);

<Timepicker variant="compactField" value={time} onChange={setTime} />;
```

#### With customization (composition)

```tsx
// Without icon
<Timepicker variant="compactField" value={time} onChange={setTime}>
  <Timepicker.CompactFieldDisplay showIcon={false} />
</Timepicker>

// Custom icon
<Timepicker variant="compactField" value={time} onChange={setTime}>
  <Timepicker.CompactFieldDisplay iconName="notification" />
</Timepicker>
```

## Context Architecture

The timepicker uses a **split context pattern** for optimal re-render performance. State is divided into 3 contexts based on update frequency:

| Context                   | Contains                                                      | Updates when...                         | Hook                         |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `TimepickerConfigContext` | `format`, `minuteInterval`, `disabled`, `readonly`, `error`   | Props change (rare)                     | `useTimepickerConfig()`      |
| `TimepickerStateContext`  | `isFocused`, `isPickerOpen`, `hasValue`, handlers, animations | Focus, picker open/close, empty↔filled | `useTimepickerInteraction()` |
| `TimepickerValueContext`  | `selectedTime`, `formattedValue`, `setTime`                   | Every time selection (hot path)         | `useTimepickerValue()`       |

**Which hook each component uses:**

| Component               | Hooks Used                                                              | Re-renders on time selection? |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `ClockIcon`             | `useTimepickerConfig`                                                   | No                            |
| `InputFieldLabel`       | `useTimepickerInteraction`                                              | No (only on empty↔filled)    |
| `InputFieldDisplay`     | `useTimepickerConfig`, `useTimepickerInteraction`, `useTimepickerValue` | Yes (needs formatted value)   |
| `InputFieldContainer`   | `useTimepickerConfig`, `useTimepickerInteraction`                       | No                            |
| `CompactFieldContainer` | `useTimepickerInteraction`                                              | No                            |
| `CompactFieldDisplay`   | `useTimepickerConfig`, `useTimepickerInteraction`, `useTimepickerValue` | Yes (needs formatted value)   |
| `HelperText`            | `useTimepickerConfig`                                                   | No                            |

